WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
I'm Patrick and Ben Cooper. Today is May 15th, 2026. Let's close out the week with today's

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.820
Tesla news. Kazakhstan's first official use of cyber trucks for state security shows how the

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:18.020
vehicles off-road and power capabilities are moving into government operations. Kazakhstan has

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.700
deployed cyber trucks for state security duties at the Turkic Summit. The vehicles will handle rapid

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.740
response, field coordination, and command tasks in mountainous terrain near Almaty.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.660
Officials noted the truck's off-road mobility, quiet electric drive for discrete movement,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:41.120
and on-board power for sustained equipment use. This marks one of the earliest documented cases

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.920
of a cyber truck entering active state security service. Now moving to charging operations,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:53.220
Tesla's virtual supercharger Q-pilot is now live at five stations in California and New York.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.500
Drivers receive an automatic wait list with estimated times instead of circling the lot.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.060
The system reduces uncertainty at busy locations and supplies Tesla with real-time demand pattern data.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.680
Brotter rollout details remain pending. Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.620
the quiet rollout of a virtual Q at select superchargers challenges the assumption

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:22.500
that charging congestion is purely a hardware problem. The pilot at five stations replaces

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.120
driver guesswork with an automatic wait list and estimated times, giving Tesla direct visibility

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:34.060
into dwell patterns and peak loads that were previously invisible. This data layer matters because

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:40.040
each additional minute of vehicle occupies a stall produces the effective capacity of the entire network

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.180
without any new concrete or steel being poured. If the system scales, Tesla's vertical integration

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:52.140
of software, payments, and site operations could turn a recurring pain point into a managed service

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:57.720
that competitors without the same control cannot easily copy, shifting the competitive edge from

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:04.500
simply building more stalls to orchestrating their use more efficiently. Newport is adding four more

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.780
Tesla model Y vehicles to its police fleet. The city will expand its existing Tesla patrol cars with

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:16.720
these additional units. The decision follows lower operating costs and simpler maintenance requirements.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.720
The move forms part of a broader municipal shift toward electric vehicles.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:27.680
In China, Tesla has fallen outside the top 10 new energy vehicle brands for April.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:34.180
BYD captured 21.4% of the market while Tesla slipped from its prior ranking.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:40.820
The result reflects stronger local competition on price and range. Tesla will need refreshed

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:47.380
local offerings to regain ground in its second largest market. SpaceX could release its IPO

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:53.360
prospectus as soon as next week. Filing documents may appear within days, shortening a timeline

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:59.960
previously described as further out. The timing influences how investors view the broader musk-linked

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:05.940
portfolio that includes Tesla. Australian owners have filed defect claims against Tesla,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.960
the legal proceedings center on specific component issues. These cases could affect warranty and

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.980
service practices in the region. The outcome may set precedents for other markets. New York

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:24.600
rebate records show $77.8 million in prior state incentives tied to earlier Tesla purchases.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.620
The data now influences resale valuations for used Model 3 and Model Y vehicles.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:37.000
Buyers and sellers must adjust expectations around fair market prices once those earlier supports

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:42.420
become visible. Tesla is promoting same-day Cybertruck demo drives through its standard

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:48.020
reservation system. The effort aims to convert interest into orders as production capacity

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:52.840
continues to grow. The move follows recent government adoption news for the vehicle.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:58.520
One development worth watching is the institutional interest reflected in recent filings.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:03.560
Meridian financial partners added to its Tesla holdings in the latest period.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:10.280
Such moves continue even as the stock trades in a defined range. Tesla has ended production of some

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:16.160
models as capacity-focused shifts. Freed resources are being redirected toward newer programs.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.740
There is a challenge worth discussing in the competitive landscape.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.820
Tesla slipped outside China's top 10 new energy vehicle brands last month,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.800
as BYD took the lead with more than one-fifth of the market.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.580
The shift highlights how quickly domestic competitors have scaled both product range

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:39.920
and pricing power. Tesla will need to respond with refreshed local offerings or adjusted positioning

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:46.000
to regain ground in its second largest market. Before we go, keep an eye on whether other

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.260
government's signal interest in Cybertruck deployments following Kazakhstan's move.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:05:01.140
That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $250.35, up $2.23, 0.9%.

